<!--
============================================
QML RESOURCE FILE
============================================

PURPOSE:
Embed QML files into the executable binary

ADVANTAGES:
✅ Single executable (no external QML files)
✅ Faster loading (no file I/O)
✅ Protection (QML code compiled into binary)
✅ Deployment (no missing file errors)

USAGE:
In C++: QUrl url("qrc:/qml/filename.qml");
In QML: import "qrc:/qml/"

PREFIX:
"/" → Root of resource system
Access via: qrc:/qml/...
-->

<RCC>
    <qresource prefix="/">
        <!-- ======================== -->
        <!-- QML VIEW FILES           -->
        <!-- ======================== -->
        <file>qml/TodoListView.qml</file>
        <file>qml/StudentTableView.qml</file>
        <file>qml/FileSystemTreeView.qml</file>
        <file>qml/EmployeeSqlView.qml</file>
        <file>qml/ProductFilterProxyView.qml</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>

<!--
============================================
📚 RESOURCE SYSTEM SUMMARY
============================================

1. WHAT IS .qrc?
   - XML file listing resources to embed
   - Processed by Qt's rcc (Resource Compiler)
   - Generates C++ code with embedded data
   - Linked into executable

2. PREFIX:
   <qresource prefix="/foo">
     <file>bar.qml</file>
   </qresource>
   
   Access: qrc:/foo/bar.qml

3. ALIASES (optional):
   <file alias="myfile.qml">actual/path/file.qml</file>
   Access: qrc:/myfile.qml

4. CMake INTEGRATION:
   Qt5: qt5_add_resources(RESOURCES qml.qrc)
   Qt6: qt_add_resources(executable qml.qrc)

5. ADVANTAGES:
   ✅ Portable - No external file dependencies
   ✅ Fast - No disk I/O at runtime
   ✅ Secure - Files embedded in binary
   ✅ Cross-platform - Works everywhere

6. WHEN TO USE:
   ✅ Production builds
   ✅ QML files
   ✅ Images, icons
   ✅ Configuration files
   ✅ Translations (.qm files)

7. WHEN NOT TO USE:
   ❌ Large media files (videos)
   ❌ User-editable content
   ❌ Frequently changing files
   ❌ Development (slower build times)

============================================
-->
